{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957406-changing-alone","id":957406,"title":"Changing alone?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-24T22:02:27-07:00","id":957406,"title":"Changing alone?","content":"So, as of 2e, the pack and the hunt are even more important to any given Uratha, regardless of personal feelings. They lose essence and harmony for going too long without hunting, and the group dynamic is pretty much required in the setting. Despite werewolf population being up to ST and prone to variety, it's assumed that any given newbie will be quickly discovered by his fellows and &quot;educated&quot;, about either Luna's glory or Tyranny, and put in a pack.<br /> <br /> That being said, what happens to a newly changed werewolf isolated from the Fosaken as a whole? Auspice is natural, and the default is Ghost Wolf, but where do they go from there? A Lune might hand out the first renown just for what happened Changing related to the lunar phase, but where do the gifts and rites come up? And if, for whatever reason, they aren't &quot;born&quot; with the Sacred Hunt rite (Luna is crazy and capricious, after all), do they just live on as a maladjusted human, ignoring their nature? Where, between first Change and standard creation rules, do we get the other benefits (ignoring tribal perks)?<br /> <br /> I ask because I've always enjoyed &quot;Lone Wolf&quot; characters, in any setting, and see no way for that to exist with the current ruleset. I understand that it's going against the design to use such a character, but find myself hoping an alternative is offered. If you had a hermit in the mountains, or on some island (stacking the deck against forsaken OR pure intervention, admittedly), and found these new abilities, what would his next step be?<br /> <br /> P.S. let it be known that i have yet to read The Pack, and may find answers there. I have, however, searched these forums, and found no information directly relevant, at least, not in a way i could tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12318-gaius94","user":"Gaius94","date":".  Thought of addition after the fact 08-25-2016, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12318-gaius94","name":"Gaius94","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T22:54:55-07:00","id":957423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius94</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957406-changing-alone#post957406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspice is natural, and the default is Ghost Wolf, but where do they go from there? A Lune might hand out the first renown just for what happened Changing related to the lunar phase, but where do the gifts and rites come up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Providing they're lucky, they would be found by a spirit who would guide them the right way. A follower of one of the Firstborn or a lune, a werewolf ancestor spirit or something similar could bring them into a tribe. The starting Gifts represent those earned through Renown, and that doesn't require other Forsaken. Spirits can teach rites as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if, for whatever reason, they aren't &quot;born&quot; with the Sacred Hunt rite (Luna is crazy and capricious, after all), do they just live on as a maladjusted human, ignoring their nature? Where, between first Change and standard creation rules, do we get the other benefits (ignoring tribal perks)? </div> </div> </div>They could. If they don't get lucky, they could end up in a really bad place. There's an entire world of beings, most of which hate werewolves, who would love to find one they could take control of or simply eliminate. If somehow any of the myriad of werewolf antagonists didn't notice this character, including the Pure, they might just drift towards Harmony 10 and fall into Kuruth at the drop of a hat. It's more likely that something would take advantage of the ignorant werewolf, like a spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I ask because I've always enjoyed &quot;Lone Wolf&quot; characters, in any setting, and see no way for that to exist with the current ruleset. I understand that it's going against the design to use such a character, but find myself hoping an alternative is offered. If you had a hermit in the mountains, or on some island (stacking the deck against forsaken OR pure intervention, admittedly), and found these new abilities, what would his next step be? </div> </div> </div>The mechanics are all there, but to be fair you're not just talking about a lone wolf. A werewolf could change, find out about its heritage from another werewolf, then go out alone in the world and be a lone wolf. Or to be picked up when the news breaks about some giant werewolf-like creature raging through a city, taught the rules, then left on their own. Without any contact with werewolves at all, you're talking more about something like an 'only wolf.'<br /> <br /> For the rite, it's all covered on p139 of the second edition book. 'A werewolf usually learns of a new rite through an Uratha or spirit teacher. Sometimes werewolves record rites on cuneiform cylinders or charred, sigil-scratched bones.' Gifts are given by spirits.<br /> <br /> Yes, such a character would have it hard, but they have isolated themselves from all of humanity and are going to have a hard time werewolf or not.<br /> <br /> PS: Regarding the Pack. Second edition's core makes it clear you can have wolf-blooded and humans in your pack, and hints at other beings. The Pack expands on that and explains what it's like to have members of the other supernatural games as packmates, as well as natural wolves and spirits. One could be the only werewolf in town but still have an extensive pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-25-2016, 02:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T01:29:04-07:00","id":957465,"title":"","content":"That makes things a little clearer. I'll admit that i exaggerated the example scenario to avoid rogue variables, and likely hurt my own interest doing so; I'm not against meeting the rest of the spirit world, i just wondered how things would go discovering this nature without an immediate education by peers. Isolation seemed like the easiest justification for having someone &quot;learn the ropes&quot; solo. Becoming prey for the first clever spirit sounds about right. I also appreciate hearing the worst case scenario for true isolation, as it really hits home the necessity for cooperation, and gives me ideas for NPCs to boot.<br /> <br /> That being said, the question does end up boiling down to figuring out the best way to run &quot;learn your heritage, join the forsaken, then wander off alone&quot;, and whether or not running without a pack is a functional option (beyond role-playing), or simply a severe handicap. Has anyone run a character like this, PC or NPC? If so, how did it go?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12318-gaius94","name":"Gaius94","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T08:55:02-07:00","id":957644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius94</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957406-changing-alone?p=957465#post957465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes things a little clearer. I'll admit that i exaggerated the example scenario to avoid rogue variables, and likely hurt my own interest doing so; I'm not against meeting the rest of the spirit world, i just wondered how things would go discovering this nature without an immediate education by peers. Isolation seemed like the easiest justification for having someone &quot;learn the ropes&quot; solo. Becoming prey for the first clever spirit sounds about right. I also appreciate hearing the worst case scenario for true isolation, as it really hits home the necessity for cooperation, and gives me ideas for NPCs to boot.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's implied a lot of Ghost Wolves find themselves in this situation, and that's how certain Lodges start up like the Temple of Apollo, detailed in the Pack. Werewolves don't know about their heritage so they just stumble into the wrong hands. Not necessarily something that wants to destroy them, but appreciates them as a being that can go back and forth between worlds and needs to 'hunt.' There's an example in the first edition books of a man who was turning in times when there were less than average numbers of werewolves. As a doctor he thought he was having a psychotic break and tried to stall it as much as he could through the use of drugs, but it kept coming. Eventually a spirit, or something like one, came and offered to help take the problem out of his hands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That being said, the question does end up boiling down to figuring out the best way to run &quot;learn your heritage, join the forsaken, then wander off alone&quot;, and whether or not running without a pack is a functional option (beyond role-playing), or simply a severe handicap. Has anyone run a character like this, PC or NPC? If so, how did it go? </div> </div> </div>I know it's been done and I've done a couple in one-on-one games. It does work as a handicap, if you're just running a single werewolf, since most of the 'standard' antagonists of the game can be pretty deadly to entire packs and just being a single character either makes things incredibly risky, demands you be really good at fighting, or flesh out your pack with other strong things, which can put a burden on the Storyteller. But if you're dealing with non-standard threats and your Storyteller doesn't mind, then you're set. And that's a reasonable option, smaller-scale games or games which put the focus elsewhere. Bans and banes become a lot more important.<br /> <br /> There's lots of ways it can happen in-game. Some werewolves are nomadic, passing through and getting new werewolves out of newbie mode then moving on, sometimes a pack dies, leaving their totem spirit wanting to guide another werewolf. Maybe the lone wolf is moving through and the pack that taught them doesn't have room for more or want to share, sends the wolf out to find their own territory at home. If they had parents its possible the parents told them or warned them what was coming before it happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T21:26:19-07:00","id":959656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius94</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957406-changing-alone?p=957465#post957465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, the question does end up boiling down to figuring out the best way to run &quot;learn your heritage, join the forsaken, then wander off alone&quot;, and whether or not running without a pack is a functional option (beyond role-playing), or simply a severe handicap. Has anyone run a character like this, PC or NPC? If so, how did it go?</div> </div> </div> </div>Viskarenvisla is actually running a great actual play for a lone wolf over at RPGNet. She hates the Forsaken because of events surrounding her first change, and doesn't think much more highly of the Pure. She had a powerful patron spirit explain the shadow to her. Her pack consists of one in the know wolfblooded and then a bunch of spirits. She has to fight smart, but she can hold her own. There is also an interesting NPC in that game who is a werewolf that got entangled with what seems like a hunter conspiracy and doesn't know ANYTHING about Spirits or the shadow. It's a great read and has recently resumed updating. They use some house rules, which changes things.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?775548-Werewolf-the-Forsaken-The-Seventh-Seal\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php...e-Seventh-Seal</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/830599-presenting-my-werewolf-ap-the-seventh-seal\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/830599-presenting-my-werewolf-ap-the-seventh-seal\"> Presenting my Werewolf AP - The Seventh Seal - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/830599-presenting-my-werewolf-ap-the-seventh-seal\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/830599-presenting-my-werewolf-ap-the-seventh-seal </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Dear friends, I'd like to humbly submit this game, played between myself and my dear friend Mr. Shopping (whom you may recognize as the ST from Detroit Rock City http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?446663-Werewolf-The-Forsaken-quot-Detroit-Rock-City-quot), as an example of Werewolf 2nd ed, but with a number of changes and leftovers from 1st ed that I liked, such as the harmony system and certain aspects of the background story. http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?775548-Werewolf-the-Forsaken-The-Seventh-Seal This game takes place in January of 2015 in the Windy City, a year after interpack conflict </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T08:47:04-07:00","id":959843,"title":"","content":"Apparently the large amount of bale hound packs in the UK is from situations like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}